# Project 2 — SSH & Remote Administration

## Overview

This project focused on configuring and testing Secure Shell (SSH) on a Raspberry Pi 5 to allow secure remote administration from another computer on the local network.

The goal was to learn how SSH works, configure an SSH server, identify the Raspberry Pi's network address, remotely connect to the system, verify remote access, and begin implementing SSH key authentication.

---

## Objectives

- Install and configure OpenSSH Server
- Enable SSH as a system service
- Identify the Raspberry Pi's LAN IP address
- Connect remotely using SSH
- Verify remote system access
- Generate an ED25519 SSH key pair
- Transfer the public key to the Raspberry Pi
- Understand password vs. key-based authentication
- Learn the basics of SSH security hardening

