# Problems Encountered

## Incorrect IP Address

Initially, the command:

```bash
hostname -I
```

displayed:

```text
192.168.122.1
```

This was identified as the libvirt virtual network address rather than the Raspberry Pi's normal LAN address.

The following command was used to identify the correct network interface:

```bash
ip -br addr
```

This revealed:

```text
wlan0    UP    10.0.0.98/24
```

The correct LAN address was therefore:

```text
10.0.0.98
```

---

## Multiple Network Interfaces

The Raspberry Pi was also running a virtual machine through libvirt.

This created an additional virtual network:

```text
virbr0 → 192.168.122.1
```

This demonstrated the importance of understanding network interfaces and IP addressing when troubleshooting connectivity.

